    "title": "State Police Honor Retired Trooper Ondus at Service - NewsBreak",
    "text": "2 hours ago Services were held Tuesday in Eden for a former law enforcement officer who served in northern Chautauqua and Cattaraugus counties, as well as southern Erie County. New York State Police honored Mark Ondus, a Gowanda native who dedicated 26 years of service to the State Police before his retirement in 2010. He served in Troop A, and later in Troop T at the SP Dunkirk barracks. He was also a member of the Gowanda Police Department and a school resource officer in North Collins. Ondus passed away last week from an illness that stemmed from his response to the 9/11 terror attacks on the World Trade Center. In a Facebook post, State Police said, \"Trooper Ondus will always be remembered as a devoted husband, father, friend, and public servant whose bravery and integrity embodied the finest traditions of the State Police.\" Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
